UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.62.2:
• Tutorial: it is offered once to every player who has not seen it yet, even with an existing progression (before, only brand-new players got it). « Skip the tutorial » is still offered at the start.
• SEGMENTS: the « World record » column is also shown for community levels (the checked record of the same version, read from its replay).

Version 2.62.1:
• Sum of Best (SOB) across everything: the best time of each segment counts, whether it was set in a full run or in section training (same level version) — training screen, Statistics (chart included), ghost panel and segment summary. The record, the segment times and the consistency stay those of full runs.
• Section training › “Watch”: your best segments one after the other, each played back exactly from the replay of the run or training attempt that set it; at each cut, “Segment 2 · training on 17/11 · 0:23.45” or “run on 12/11”, and a timer that adds up to the sum of best, compared with the record. Play, pause, previous / next segment, speed, with keyboard, gamepad and mouse.
• End of run › Segments, online: a “World record · name” column with the splits of the verified world record of the same level version (read from its verified replay, never a pending record), duration and cumulative gap; “loading…” during the request, no column offline; if it was already a ghost of the run, its column is renamed.
• The best segments'' replays stay on this computer (never sent, nothing ranked) as long as a best segment refers to them. A best time set before this version has no replay — unless it comes from your record, the previous one or your last run, found at the exact time: the montage says so instead of inventing it.

Version 2.62.0:
• Administration › Assets: every file of the game (images, animations, sounds, music, fonts, data), sorted in a tree — Characters, Enemies, Bosses and giga bosses by world, Powers, Scenery and tiles by planet, Interface and icons, Effects and particles, Stories, Music by jukebox group, Sounds, Fonts —, each folder with its number of assets and its weight.
• Instant search (name, path, folder, type, “used by”), filters by type and “Unused”; results as a grid of thumbnails or as a list, only the visible thumbnails are loaded.
• Preview of the chosen asset: image on a checkerboard, playing animation (clip, frames per second), sounds and music to listen to (the menu music waits, then resumes), font and text; size, dimensions, frames and clips, length.
• Used by: the enemies, bosses, levels (with the count), planets, powers, stories, suits, effects, jukebox tracks and the code that use it; each line shows what this “user” uses, “Sheet” opens its sheet in the game, “Open the folder” the file on the PC. Read only.
• Boss statistics › Sheet: each attack unfolds and folds (a click, Enter or A; « Unfold all », « Fold all »). Unfolded, it says what it does and gives its characteristics read from the boss''s definition: damage, wind-up and cooldown in each phase where it comes, recovery, reach and what its type uses (projectiles, speed, duration, radius…).
• Each unfolded attack has its animated example, played by the game engine: the boss in its arena, at the phase where the attack comes (its last stand for the attacks of its final scene), uses it in a loop, and Nova shows how to dodge it when it is simple. One example at a time: that of the unfolded attack that has the selection, or of the last one unfolded.
• The example is prepared without freezing the screen (a message says so meanwhile), pauses with a click, and never counts: no records, no statistics, no achievements. Every boss gets it: the planets'' bosses, the guardians of Aethra, the giga bosses of Les Confins and Singularis.
• Administration › Creations › Studio: a real editor to draw the creations'' images. On the left the explorer (the server''s suits, trails, frames and victory effects and this PC''s drafts, search, new, duplicate, rename, archive, library); at the top the tabs of the open creations (● not saved, closing confirmed); in the middle the canvas, with zoom, grid, onion skin and coordinates, and its tools: pencil, eraser, paint bucket, eyedropper, line, rectangle, ellipse, selection, move, mirrors and symmetry, undo / redo (Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y); on the right the palette (the creation''s, Nova''s, the planets''), the HSV picker, the #rrggbb code and the live preview.
• A suit is drawn frame by frame on Nova''s sheet: the timeline shows each animation of the game (idle, run, jump…) and its frames, with playback, onion skin and "Recolour all the frames…" at once (one colour for another, or a suit''s three colours).
• A trail or a victory effect becomes an animated particle and its emitter (particles per second, lifetime, size, speed, spread, gravity, rotation, fade, colours from start to end, sparkles); a frame, a ring drawn around the avatar. Previews: Nova running, her ghost, the effect replayed at the exit, the frame on the profile and in a leaderboard.
• Import an image: drag a PNG into the window, choose it, or drop it in the game''s "Images to import" folder, which the Studio watches. Cut by automatic detection of the zones, by a regular grid or by hand; each row goes to the animation of your choice, with an animated preview before importing; a refused file says why. Ctrl+Z undoes the whole import.
• "Save" keeps a draft on this PC; "Send to the server" publishes the creation and its image: the server checks the PNG (signature, dimensions, size), keeps it under its fingerprint and writes every sending and every refusal to the Log. The games download the image of a creation you won, or that appears in a leaderboard, a profile or a challenge''s rewards, keep it for offline play and draw the simple look while it is missing.
• Exclusive items: what can only be won as the reward of a challenge (the creations of Cosmic Online and the challenge rewards of the Wardrobe) wears a golden aura that gently pulses around its thumbnail, in the Wardrobe, the new rewards screen, the rewards of a challenge and the end of a challenge. Its tooltip, with the mouse, the keyboard or the gamepad, says where it comes from: “Exclusive: daily challenge of 10/11/2026 · Gold reached”.
• Administration › Creations: the game''s reserve, 40 suits, 30 trails, 30 frames and 30 victory effects with carefully chosen names and colours, ready to be given as the reward of a challenge (Challenge calendar › Rewards). A filter and a label for each creation: reserve (never given), given as a reward, archived.
• A creation stays hidden from the players until a challenge that has begun gives it or someone has won it: the reserve and the rewards of the coming challenges are not revealed ahead of time.
• The story of Pyrrhax, “The Obsidian Dragon”, becomes a short cartoon: its six shots are animated scenes made of real sprites in the game''s style — Smoky and his fire brothers and sisters, the egg hatching in the nest of ashes, the flames, the smoke, the rain of embers, the belly lighting up, the change into a dragon of black glass, then the great Pyrrhax before the last frontier.
• Every character plays its animations frame by frame (hatching, fire breath, cloud of smoke, coughing, swallowed embers, transformation, roar), and the scenery is alive too: twinkling stars, drifting clouds and mist, magma breathing at the foot of the spires, embers crackling on the ground, ash blown by the wind, glows and shadows following the fire. The layers scroll at their own speed, the camera follows the action, the screen shakes and lights up in time with the text, which stays as long to read as before.
• To watch it again: Collection › Gallery › Bosses, or the boss statistics (“Watch the story again”); a NEW pill leads you there.
• Clans come to Cosmic Online (ONLINE › CLANS): one clan per player, 50 members at most, a name, a unique tag of 2 to 5 letters or digits (shown in brackets, [DAWN]), a motto and an emblem (a shape and two colours).
• Roles: a chief (who can hand their role over), officers and members. The chief and the officers invite, accept or decline applications and exclude (an officer does not exclude an officer, nobody excludes the chief); the chief appoints the officers, edits the clan and can disband it.
• Joining by invitation, by application (with a short message) or open to everyone, as the chief chooses; invitations are accepted from the CLANS screen or from their notification.
• A clan''s page: its members and their role (their presence only for the clan''s members, and only if the player shares it), its best team on every EXTREME level (Solo for now, Duo and Trio co-op is coming soon), the applications (chief and officers) and the clan''s chat, also in SOCIAL.
• Clan ranking: the sum of each clan''s best results verified by the server on the EXTREME levels; the clan''s tag shows next to the username in the leaderboards, the profile and SOCIAL.
• Administration › Clans: an admin renames or disbands a clan; every action is written to the Log.
• Update notification: it shows what changed in every version published since the player''s (including versions without an installer of their own), not only the latest one.' WHERE version = '2.62.2';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.62.3:
• Ambushes: falling during an ambush no longer restarts it. It waits for Nova as she left it (same wave, defeated enemies stay defeated, the others stay where they are with their health); its doors open to let her back in and close behind her. An ambush enemy that leaves its arena is brought back into it: the ambush can always be finished. Records kept.
• HUD: “Ambush: N enemies left” (and the current wave) during an ambush, to place or hide in the HUD editor; violet arrows toward its enemies off screen (Settings › Game › Arrows toward off-screen enemies).' WHERE version = '2.62.3';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.63.1:
• The Phoenix''s story, “The Dawn Bearer”, becomes a little cartoon too: the little bird of light leaving the star of the centre, its flight over the sleeping volcanoes and the valleys of black glass where day breaks behind it, the long night it waits through on its crag, its feathers catching fire until it falls into ashes, its rebirth bigger and brighter, then the Phoenix burning itself away in its nest on the peak. Living scenery (dawn breaking, smoking volcanoes, glittering glass, mist), characters animated frame by frame; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.

Version 2.63.0:
• New: co-op on the EXTREME levels, with 2 or 3 players (main menu › Co-op). One life each, the same rules as in solo; on one PC (one gamepad per player besides the keyboard), on the local network (one PC hosts, no account nor server) or online with your friends (lobby, invitations, "Ready").
• No friendly fire: attacks and powers only hit enemies. Players are solid, without pushing: an ally stops you like a wall, and you can stand on their head (if they leave, you fall). Enemies aim at the nearest player; their blows hit everyone they reach.
• Revival: a downed player leaves their soul; an ally who stays near it for 2 s revives them (2 revivals per team and per attempt). Everyone down at once: the attempt stops. The camera frames the whole team; a player off screen for 3 s comes back near the nearest ally.
• Disconnection: the player goes on standby (untouchable, in nobody''s way); they have 60 s to come back: their game catches up at high speed, then they reappear near the team. Otherwise the team goes on, ranked "incomplete".
• Verification race: Solo, Duo and Trio tabs, which never mix. A team is ranked by its most advanced player (ties: fewer revivals, then the earliest); the server checks every attempt with each player''s inputs and path, and each player confirms it with their own account. A game on one PC is not ranked (an account only opens on its own computer). All solo records stay valid.
• Team replays: the viewer follows the whole team or the player of your choice.

Version 2.62.5:
• The Kraken''s story, “The Lantern of the depths”, becomes a little cartoon too: the egg hatching in the black sea under the crust of the Confins, the little octopus with one lit arm, the lost fish following its light to the hot springs, the star''s light falling into the sea in sparks, its eight arms lighting up one by one, the fish fleeing from its shadow into the cracks, then the Kraken waiting at the bottom of the Trench. Living scenery (rays of light, drifting silt, swaying kelp, jellyfish, glowing reefs), characters animated frame by frame; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.

Version 2.62.4:
• The Monolith''s story, “The Primordial Golem”, becomes a little cartoon too: the pebble tumbling in the dust of the beginning, the children of the cave carving their rune on it, the stone growing generation after generation before it stands up, the village and its fire, the ships leaving for the stars, then the golem alone in the ruins facing a visitor it does not recognise. Living scenery (breathing crystals, torches, mist, dust), characters animated frame by frame, a camera that follows the action; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.' WHERE version = '2.63.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.63.5:
• Singularis''s story, “The Collapsed Heart”, becomes a little cartoon too: Lyse, the very young star at the centre of Kepler-Voss, her song of light with three little planets turning round her, her gifts (sap, fire, the glitter of ice) making them bloom, the machines come to drink her light, the last spark shivering with cold, then the collapse and Singularis waking up hungry, pulling everything in. Living space (a turning nebula, twinkling stars, veils of dust, debris), characters animated frame by frame; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.

Version 2.63.4:
• Small texts (1280×720 windows and smaller): the spaces between words no longer disappear.

Version 2.63.3:
• The Titan''s story, “The Last Shift”, becomes a little cartoon too: the foundry under the Confins with its furnaces, the crucible pouring steel and the workers hammering, the colossus waking up on its scaffold, the foreman entrusting it with the fires on the night the star collapses, the rock swallowing the foundry while it tends the fires alone, the rust and the steam, then the Titan turning on the visitor come to “put out its fires”. Living scenery (roaring furnaces, gears, chains, smoke, sparks), characters animated frame by frame; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.

Version 2.63.2:
• The Lich''s story, “The Keeper of Names”, becomes a little cartoon too: old Ossian lighting a candle for each of the dead of the catacombs, the stones whose names light up as he tells them to a child, the night the star collapses and the living flee while he stays, his soul hidden in the crystal on the altar, the centuries putting out the candles and leaving only his bones and the green flame, then the Lich watching over its crypt among the names. Living scenery (niches, candles, cobwebs, mist, dust), characters animated frame by frame; a NEW pill leads to “Watch the story again”.' WHERE version = '2.63.5';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.63.9:
• Trailer: about 40 seconds of quick cuts and big titles, made of real scenes of the game — Nova running, jumping, shooting and gliding on Sylvanox, Pyralis and Glacior, the seven giga bosses roaring on the scenery of their stories, Pyrrhax''s hatchlings, three Novas in cooperation, Cosmic Online — to Singularis''s music. It starts on the title screen after 1 minute without any input (keyboard, mouse, gamepad) and loops; any key, click or movement goes straight back to the menu without triggering anything. Never while typing, with a window open, during a download or before the tutorial; Settings › Game › “Trailer on the title screen after 1 min idle” turns it off.

Version 2.63.8:
• Game update: a progress bar shows how far the installer download is (MB received / total), the download is no longer cut after 90 s on a slow connection (it only stops if nothing arrives for 60 s), and the message gives the real reason for a failure (connection too slow, no connection to the server, server error).

Version 2.63.7:
• Clans: every clan has its public sheet, like a profile (emblem, name and tag, motto, foundation date, members and roles, points and rank, best EXTREME results, « Join » or « Apply » depending on its membership mode), visible even without an account. It opens from the search, the clan ranking, a profile, or with a click on a [TAG] in the rankings and in SOCIAL.
• Player profiles: new « Clan » tab with the sheet of the player''s clan (or « This player is not in any clan »). A clan''s leader and officers find « Invite to my clan » there, greyed out with the reason when it is not possible (clan full, invitation already sent, player already in a clan, blocked player).
• CLANS: new « Management » tab for the leader and the officers: applications received (message, accept or refuse), invitations sent (player, date, who invited them, « Cancel »), members and roles, and the clan''s settings (motto, emblem and membership, handing over the leader''s role, confirmed disbanding) for the leader only.

Version 2.63.6:
• Co-op on the community''s EXTREME levels: the CO-OP lobby offers “Campaign / Community” (title, author and version of the levels installed from ONLINE LEVELS), and the page of an EXTREME level gets “Play in co-op”. Everybody plays the same version: a guest who does not have the level receives it before “Ready” (downloaded from Cosmic Online, or sent by the host PC over the local network, even without Internet), with its progress; its size is bounded and its fingerprint checked before it is installed, and a game never starts with two different versions. The Duo and Trio rankings of each version are shown on the level''s page and at the end of the game (clan points still count the official levels only).' WHERE version = '2.63.9';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.64.0:
• The seven giga bosses'' stories and the trailer now have their sound effects: an ambience under every shot (the night wind, a dripping cave, rumbling magma, the deep sea, the catacombs, the foundry, a cosmic hum) and the noises of what happens — the egg cracking, the breath of flames, stone splitting, wings, the star of the centre collapsing, bubbles, candles, bones, steam and hammers, Lyse''s song, the bosses'' roars. Placed in the picture (left, right), played on the “Effects” volume of the Settings (and muted with it); the music lowers a little under the biggest ones.
• Giga boss stories: “Skip” (Space, Enter, Ⓐ or a click) now skips only the shot playing, with a quick fade to the next one (on the last shot, the story ends); “Quit” (Esc, Ⓑ or a click on its hint) leaves the whole story.' WHERE version = '2.64.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.64.2:
• Co-op on one PC: one device per player. The keyboard and the mouse go together to one player only, each gamepad to one player only; Start or Ⓐ on a free gamepad takes a place, Ⓑ leaves it, "Change device" moves to the next free one, and the gamepad given a place rumbles once. Each card of the lobby shows its player''s device ("Xbox gamepad (no. 1)", the number kept when it is plugged back in) and lights up the buttons being pressed; the list of connected devices updates live (an unplugged gamepad stays there for a few seconds). Xbox, PlayStation, Switch (B at the bottom, A on the right, ZL / ZR, + / −) or generic glyphs.
• Gamepad unplugged in the middle of a game (alone as in co-op on one PC): the game and the timer pause and "GAMEPAD UNPLUGGED" says whose it was; plugging it back in restarts the game after 3, 2, 1. Ⓐ on another free gamepad takes the player''s place with their keys, Enter gives them the keyboard if it is free; in co-op, "Continue without…" lets the team go on without them (60 s to come back, as online). Online, the 60-second reconnection rule does not change. A gamepad''s low battery: a line in the team panel, no pause.
• Keys per player: profiles P1, P2 and P3 kept in the settings (keyboard and mouse, gamepad buttons and settings) and the power keys of each level for each of them. In co-op on one PC, "Keys of this level" has one tab per player with the keys of their device and its glyphs, conflicts checked for that device, "Copy Pn''s keys", "Default" and "Pn''s controls…" (Settings › Keyboard / Gamepad, one button per player). Alone, nothing changes.

Version 2.64.1:
• Keys: in Settings › Keyboard / mouse and Gamepad, and in « Keys of this level » (level panels, challenges, pause menu « Keys… »), the key, mouse or gamepad button, trigger or stick direction you are holding lights up live in the list, without changing anything: a way to check it is the right key. Released, it goes dark; nothing lights up while you are choosing a new key.' WHERE version = '2.64.2';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.65.0:
• Clan raids, phase 1: “ASTERION, THE DEVOURER OF WORLDS” arrives in CLANS › RAIDS. The card of the coming world event (local time and UTC, countdown, short, standard or legendary format, difficulty, registered clans and players, your clan''s registered players), the clan raids scheduled by the chief or an officer (places, registrations locked before the start), the invitations between clans to a joint raid, the clan''s history and the raid notifications panel (“Mark all read”, reminders 24 h, 1 h and 10 min as you choose, members'' registrations grouped). An event''s sheet: register and unregister, register the clan, “Invite members…”, groups of 8 with their leader, raid leader and instructions. The combat comes in a future version: nothing to win yet.
• ADMINISTRATION › Raids: schedule a world event in your own local time (stored in UTC, previewed in Paris, Montréal, São Paulo and Tokyo), set its format, lock time, capacity and difficulty, open or close its registrations, publish it to every clan or cancel it; each action goes to the Log. Every raid time follows the computer''s time zone and its daylight saving time.' WHERE version = '2.65.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.66.1:
• Asterion in real pixel art: in CLANS › RAIDS and on an event''s sheet, the titan is now a detailed sprite, part by part (Skullmaw skull, Dreadfang and Pyroclast arms, Heartbreaker torso, Voidworm abdomen, Graviton and Titanus legs, cosmic heart, aura) that breathes, whose heart beats and around which particles drift. Hover a part with the mouse or reach it with the keyboard or the gamepad: it lights up and its tooltip gives its name, its gigaboss, its state (under attack, weakened, destroyed or undiscovered) and what destroying it does to Asterion.

Version 2.66.0:
• Clan raids, phase 2: Asterion''s « RIGHT ARM » branch is playable. During a running raid, the event sheet opens the branch map: eight zones linked along the titan''s arm (the Shoulder and its three spawn points, the Basalt Biceps with its breathing platforms, the Magma Vein and its flow, the Forge Elbow and its two bellows to destroy by two groups, the secret Slag Grotto, the Forearm and its shortcut, the Lock Wrist opened by two generators, the Hand of Pyroclast sealed until the next version), their state, the objectives done and by which group, the groups and where they are, « Join » or « Help » another group.
• Combat in instances of 8 players: each group plays in input lockstep like the cooperation (joining a game in progress, 60 s to come back after a disconnection, then the place is freed), goes from zone to zone without losing its hearts or powers, with a minimap, the group panel, the zone''s objectives, the branch''s alerts and the warning of the magma flows. The server only validates an objective when the majority of the instance''s players saw exactly the same thing; an objective destroyed by two groups at the same time counts only once.' WHERE version = '2.66.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.68.0:
• Clan raids, phase 3: the gigaboss PYROCLAST waits in the Hand of Pyroclast, at the end of the « RIGHT ARM » branch. A giant magma hand that walks on its fingers, in three announced phases: « Magma fist » (punches, magma rain, eruptions, lava bombs, tremors), « Basalt carapace » (the ground gives way to magma under the towers, meteor fist) and « Magma heart » (magma tide, closing curtains of lava, double meteor fist), then a last eruption to survive. Its look changes with each phase.
• A giant for eight: Pyroclast is several times your size and its arena is more than six screens wide, with two towers of ledges above magma pits and two goods lifts up to a platform above its head. Its « Magma fists » target every player at once: a mark under each of them, then a falling fist. Its three vents are on the two towers and the platform: the group must split up.
• Gigaboss arena camera: on entering, a shot of the whole arena and the boss, then a view that follows you and widens just enough for what threatens you, the boss when it is close and your nearby allies; arrows at the edge of the screen show the boss (its weak points when it is exposed), your allies and the enemies of an ambush.
• The Lock Wrist becomes the long road to the Hand: about 15 minutes with eight players (an estimate computed from the level and checked by the tests), two-lane galleries, four giant ambushes on several floors, a double valve for 4 players, a goods lift for 3 players, twin plates to hold together and checkpoints. The Hand only opens once its lock is broken.
• Fight together: while its carapace protects it, nothing hurts it. Its three vents spit jets of magma in turn; a player standing 3 s on a vent closes it, but a closed vent lights up again after 15 s: they must be held together. All three closed, the carapace bursts: its heart is bare (double damage) and its three weak points each break for a share of its health. Its health and the pace of its attacks follow the number of players in the instance (2 to 8). Reviving a downed ally counts as a rescue.
• Contributions computed in the simulation, the same on every computer of the instance: damage (and to the gigaboss), damage avoided (its blows dodged, the blows stopped by the shield), support, vents closed, weak points broken, objectives, participation time, presence at its fall. The server only keeps a table when the majority of the instance sent the same one, refuses impossible values and logs the liars; while it waits, the result is « awaiting validation ».
• Asterion''s body: once Pyroclast''s fall is validated, the right arm shows « destroyed » on the titan (« attacked », then « weakened » during the fight), and its effect is noted on the event''s sheet: no more lava rains.
• Raid results: clan ranking and individual ranking by category (contribution, damage, damage avoided, support, objectives, gigabosses defeated, participation time, rescues, progression), opened at Pyroclast''s fall and from the event''s sheet. The contribution score mixes every category, each one capped: damage alone is never enough.
• Rewards to claim (CLANS › RAIDS and the results screen, « Claim » button): « Hand of Pyroclast » profile badge (present at its fall), « Asterion''s Assailant » title (5 minutes of fighting), « Magma Breaker » (contribution score of 1,500) and « Scourge of Pyroclast » (the event''s 3 best scores) titles. Granted by the server from validated results, only once even after a reconnection; once claimed, they unlock in the profile and the wardrobe.
• Administration › Raids: « Test Asterion » (administrators) launches any zone of a raid branch alone and locally, the Pyroclast fight included, in « Invincible (admin) · unranked » mode, with a number of simulated players (2 to 8) for its health and a starting phase. A test never counts: no report, no consensus, no ranking, no reward; the server refuses any report flagged as a test.

Version 2.67.1:
• Asterion''s mini-film: the first time you go to see the titan (CLANS › RAIDS, the sheet of an event), a cinematic of about two minutes tells who it is, in ten animated shots: the cosmic Heart beating alone in the void, its body forged from broken worlds, a planet devoured as its lights go out one by one, its seven parts and their Gigabosses revealed one by one (Skullmaw, Dreadfang, Pyroclast, Heartbreaker, Voidworm, Graviton, Titanus), our galaxy in its sights, Nova swept away by a backhand, the clans'' beacons lighting up, the hologram of its branches to bring down, its roar and the title "ASTERION — THE DEVOURER OF WORLDS", then the call: "Gather your clan. The hunt begins." With its own music and sound effects. This first showing cannot be skipped; it only counts as seen once it has played to the end (closing the game halfway plays it again next time), and that follows you to another computer with your progression. The "Watch the cinematic again" button on the event''s card plays it again whenever you like, and that one can be left.
• Comfort: the mouse pointer disappears while you play a level (campaign, co-op, raids) and comes back as soon as a menu opens (pause, results, power choice…); fullscreen (F11 or Alt+Enter) is now always borderless fullscreen at the desktop resolution, with no video mode change.

Version 2.67.0:
• Clan raids, phase 4: Asterion''s whole body is playable. Beside the Right arm, six new branches of eight zones each (56 zones in all), each with its own world, enemies, crossings and danger: Skullmaw''s SKULL (floating vertebrae, laser gazes, psychic wave), Dreadfang''s LEFT ARM (ice that gives way, turrets, claw sweep), Heartbreaker''s TORSO (moving ribs, energy barriers, heart pulse, four plates to break with several groups), Voidworm''s ABDOMEN (acid pools, parasite nest, acid reflux), Graviton''s LEFT LEG (weightless wells, shifting islets, gravity wells) and Titanus'' RIGHT LEG (giant pistons, lava, seismic wave). Each branch has two paths, a secret zone and its relic, a shortcut to open with a lever, a zone that needs two groups and a lock of several objectives; each gigaboss'' door stays sealed until the next version.
• Before each lair, a long expedition for 8 players (about 15 minutes, even with 8): three floors so nobody gets in the way, locks whose doors open on every floor when several players stand together on the plate, a goods lift that starts with several players, checkpoints on every floor (the zone starts again at the last one reached and the players who are down get up there) and four giant ambushes on the three floors at once. Behind the sealed door, each gigaboss'' arena is huge (more than two screens wide, five storeys of platforms), ready for the fights of the next version.
• The global map of the titan: the sheet of a running raid opens « Titan map », the first of the three map levels. The whole Asterion with the state of its seven branches (not discovered yet, combat in progress, weakened), the groups fighting there (your clan in gold), the progress (zones controlled out of 56, objectives, gigabosses), the effects between branches, the reinforcements needed and the alerts of the whole titan. A branch (clicked on the titan or in the list, with the keyboard or the gamepad) opens its map of eight zones.
• The branches are linked: an objective completed in one acts on another, at the same moment for every player of an instance. The Skull''s eyes put out switch off the Left arm''s turrets, its severed nerves stop the Right leg''s seismic wave, the Left leg''s generators cut make the Torso''s barriers fall, the Abdomen''s nest destroyed removes its parasite reinforcements, the Right leg''s reactors cut stop the Right arm''s magma flows, and several ways only open when another branch gives way. The server only counts the objectives validated by the consensus of each instance.
• Player placement: 8 players at most per instance, up to 50 per clan. Choose a branch (or « Join where the clan needs me »): the server places you in a group of your clan that has room, opens a new one when all are full and sends latecomers where the clan is fighting. The « Clan placement » screen shows everyone''s place; the chief, the officers and the raid leader move a player there or balance the groups of a branch.' WHERE version = '2.68.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.68.1:
• Fix: in raids and online co-op, Escape opened the pause and closed it right away; the pause now stays open. Online, it only pauses the player who asked for it (the group keeps going); the admin Asterion test, alone on its computer, stops entirely.' WHERE version = '2.68.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.69.0:
• Clan raids, phase 4B: three of Asterion''s lairs open. VOIDWORM, the worm of the void, waits at the bottom of the ABDOMEN; GRAVITON, the leg that bends space, at the end of the LEFT LEG; TITANUS, the leg that crushes everything, at the end of the RIGHT LEG. Three true raid fights in three announced phases, a last attack to survive, a look that changes at each phase, giants for eight players in arenas more than six screens wide.
• Voidworm bursts out of a pit in the middle of its lair and cuts the group in two: it burrows under every player (a mark, then a maw bursting out of the ground), aims at players with a green ring and swallows those who stay in it — the others must burst its stomach to free them before it digests them. Its parasites come out in waves (half as many if the Abdomen''s nest is destroyed) and, in its 3rd phase, the acid rises over the whole arena: only the high roots stay dry (lower still if the Intestine''s two valves are closed). In its chitin, its three hooks must be held together to pin it and open its maw.
• Graviton floats in its gravity generators and bends space by sectors: gravity turns over, you fall toward the vault whose field hurts, except under a slab that serves as a shelter; in its 3rd phase, half the arena turns over. Debris falls on every player, a gravity well opens under each one. Its four generators, in separate sectors (two up high), only shut down all AT THE SAME TIME: one player on each, and the leg collapses, its gravity cores bare (one generator less if the leg''s own are cut).
• Titanus stomps: its shockwaves run along the floor and are jumped over (the grates protect), its heel falls on every player, it charges, leaps, brings boulders down from the vault, and in its 2nd phase its heel splits the arena''s floor over the forge. Its two ankle restraints must be broken less than a second and a half apart: alone, a restraint forges again; together, they bring it to its knee, its kneecap bare (more time if the leg''s two reactors are cut).
• Each one counts for the contributions (mechanisms held, restraints broken, weak points, allies freed from Voidworm), the results validated by the majority of the instance, the titan''s map (its part destroyed at its fall) and the « Tester Asterion » tool (starting phase, invincible, never sent). Three new badges, granted only once by the server: « Voidworm''s belly », « Graviton''s foot », « Titanus''s heel ».

Version 2.68.2:
• Pause online and in tests: the pause never stops the game, not even in the admin Asterion test. Only the player who asked for it stops acting; enemies and the boss keep going and can still hit them (the pause menu says so).' WHERE version = '2.69.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.70.0:
• Clan raids, phase 5: WORLD EVENTS. Every registered clan faces the same Asterion at the same moment (UTC reference time, shown in your own time): each group of 8 plays in its own instance, but everything it validates counts for a single titan, and for its clan.
• An objective destroyed at the same moment by two groups counts only once for the world (and once for each of the two clans); a repeated, late or older report never counts twice. The server only adds up results validated by the majority of each instance.
• New “World ranking” (sheet of a world event): the world progress (objectives, zones, gigabosses defeated), the ranking of every clan, of the groups and of the players in every category (contribution, damage, damage avoided, support, objectives, time, rescues, progress), and your clan''s page. What still awaits the majority of its instance is shown apart, “awaiting validation”, and never counts as final.
• At the end of a world event, the server freezes the official result only once (ten minutes after the end, for the last reports): “Asterion has fallen” or “Asterion survived”, the world progress and each clan''s rank. Registered clans and players are told, and the raid history of CLANS › RAIDS keeps every official result.
• Exclusive rewards limited to the world event: the “Asterion Bark” suit (5 minutes of combat validated during the event) and the clan title “Devourers Devoured” for the clans of the official top 10. Granted only once by the server, to claim in CLANS › RAIDS.
• Catch-up sessions: after the official event, absent players discover the raid in their own instances (a member registers, their clan with them) and earn the silver “Asterion Bark” suit; the official result never changes.
• Late arrival: each world event says until when a player may still enter play after the start; players already placed always come back (reconnection).
• ADMINISTRATION › Raids: a “Live” tab with real figures (players connected, instances with their zone, their players and the latency measured by the games, gigabosses defeated, reconnections, refused reports) and the log of actions and anomalies; “Suspend” / “Resume” the event (the suspended time is given back); “Validate the map” (checked by the server, required to publish); “Catch-up session”; the late arrival setting. Every action goes to the Log.' WHERE version = '2.70.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.71.0:
• Clan raids, phase 4B: three new gigaboss of Asterion are fought in their lairs, at the end of their branches. SKULLMAW, the all-seeing skull (Skull), DREADFANG, the tearing claws (Left arm) and HEARTBREAKER, the cage that guards the heart (Torso): each enormous, in three announced phases, with its attacks, its danger zones, its weak points and a look that changes with its health.
• Skullmaw: a laser gaze tracks every player at once, then freezes — leave its line; under its psychic veil, its « Gaze of death » charges then blinds everyone no column hides: hold enough mirrors together (up to four with eight players) to throw its gaze back, it is blinded and its two eyes and the crystal on its brow break. At its last phase, the arena sinks into darkness and only the light of its eye reveals the platforms.
• Dreadfang: its claws burst out of the ground under each player, its sweeps cross whole storeys of the arena (jump the blade or change storey) and it nails a player to the ground whom the others must free by breaking the claw; armoured in frost, its three chains must be held together to pin it to the floor and break its joints. At its last phase, its unleashed claws shred platforms.
• Heartbreaker: its four armour plates (two high, two low) must fall together or they grow back; its heartbeats send waves along the floor in rhythm to jump over, rib traps snap shut around each player, and to strike the light of its heart its ribs must be pried open from both sides at once.
• Each gigaboss defeated destroys its part of the titan and gives its badge (« Skullmaw''s gaze », « Dreadfang''s claws », « Heartbreaker''s cage ») to the players present at its fall, only once; the mechanisms held, the allies freed and the blows dodged count in the contributions. The administrators'' « Test Asterion » tool offers their three fights.
• Gigaboss fixes: a player swallowed by Voidworm no longer gets a « Burrowing » mark and is no longer hit inside its stomach; at the end of their exposure, Voidworm, Graviton and Titanus now re-form their carapace instead of staying vulnerable until the end of the fight.
• Administration › Assets: every new asset carries the « NEW » badge on its thumbnail or its row until it gets the focus or a click; its folders in the tree, the Assets tab and the Administration entry keep it while an asset under them is new. The version in which each asset appeared is computed automatically (tools/assets/asset_versions.py, run again with code_refs.py).' WHERE version = '2.71.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.72.0:
• Aimed attack: hold Up while attacking to strike above Nova, on the ground as in the air; in the air, hold Down to strike below. On the ground, Down stays « crouch » (the attack then strikes forwards, as before) and, with the Seismic Slam, Down + Attack in the air stays the seismic slam. These strikes hit enemies (same damage, same knockback) and breakable objects like the forward strike, with their own animations and blade arc; a strike downwards in the air still bounces off the enemy it hits and gives back the air jumps, as before. The direction is the one chosen when the strike starts. Explained in Settings › Keyboard / mouse and Gamepad, and in the tutorial.
• Records and rankings kept: nothing is reset. Replays recorded before this version play back exactly as before (with the rules of their time); new replays note the version of the simulation that played them. Suits created online keep their sheet: during a strike upwards or downwards, Nova shows the forward strike in them.
• The game''s presentation (README) and its documentation now show the clan raids and co-op in short films recorded in the game: three players together on an EXTREME level, the fights against Pyroclast and Graviton, Asterion''s appearance and the titan''s map; every documentation page has its pictures and its “← Back” link.' WHERE version = '2.72.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.73.1:
• Who is online in your clan: in CLANS › Members, each member wears the presence pill of SOCIAL (online, away, offline), the online members come first, and the list''s header shows « X/Y online ».
• Raid sheet: your clan''s registrants also wear their presence pill in their group, and « CLAN REGISTRANTS » shows how many are online. A hidden presence (« Show my presence to my friends » unticked) shows as offline; only the clan''s members see it.
• The pill at the top right of the COSMIC ONLINE screens now shows the real latency to the server: « Online - 25ms », measured on the game''s light exchanges (presence heartbeat, connection check), smoothed over the last ones; « Online » alone until a first measure exists.

Version 2.73.0:
• Clan raids, phase 7: reliability. If your link with the instance''s relay drops, the game reconnects by itself during the 60 seconds your seat waits for you: the world stays shown under the « LINK LOST » card, then you rejoin your group after catching up, without going back through the branch map.
• Clan raids: an instance no longer stops when the whole group loses its connection at the same time; it waits 60 seconds for its players. It also survives a restart of the server relaying it: the game is saved every second and everyone finds it again on their return.
• Clan raids: restarting the game or changing networks in the middle of a fight no longer locks you out; your new connection takes your seat back.
• Clan raids: a stronger consensus against cheating. Only the players really in play vote, a false report arriving at the same moment as the validation is refused and logged, nothing is accepted any more after a world event closes, and a group no longer moves back on the map when two reports arrive out of order.
• Clan raids: tested at a large scale (four clans of 50 players at once, a world event of 2,500 players): no registration, seat, reward or notification twice, and the server does the same work per request with 2 or 30 groups.' WHERE version = '2.73.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.73.2:
• Clan raids: the arrows toward off-screen monsters are back in raids, exactly as in the levels: orange arrows toward the enemies already seen, violet arrows toward those of the ambush under way, with their number, besides the arrows toward the gigaboss and your allies.
• Clan raids: a zone keeps what the group did in it. Coming back to a zone (or when the whole group falls and the zone starts again), the doors and passages opened, the levers, the generators, the arenas and ambushes cleared, the guardians and enemies beaten, the relics taken, the group plates and the last checkpoint stay as you left them. What another group validated applies too (a guardian it beat is no longer there).
• Admin test “Test Asterion”: it plays like a real instance. The branch''s state carries from one zone to the next (as the server sends it in a raid), and the simulated players are real, visible companions named “Simulated player 2”, “Simulated player 3”… with their colour in the group panel: they follow you, jump the gaps, strike the nearby enemies, stand on the plates, the lifts and the vents with you, revive the players down and flee the magma. The mechanisms for several players therefore work alone. A test still sends nothing to the server.
• The raid minimap redone in textures: readable rock and ledges, lava, the area the magma floods, open or locked passages, doors, objectives (to do, done, optional), checkpoints, group plates, vents, enemies, bosses, allies in their colour and you in gold, with a small measured legend.
• Large raid map: press M (or View / Back on a gamepad; the key can be changed in Settings › Controls, a mouse button works too) to enlarge the map over almost the whole screen: the whole zone (or a window that follows you with an overview of the whole zone), the branch''s zones and their state, the full legend. It never pauses the game: the group keeps playing. The key is recalled in the raid''s pause.
• HUD editor: a new “Raids” tab, a layout apart from the levels'' one. Place, resize, show or hide the minimap, the group panel (8 players), the objectives and the branch''s progress, the gigaboss bar, the alerts, the contributions, the “TEST ADMIN” badge, your health and your powers, and turn the off-screen arrows on or off. The preview shows an example of a raid with 8 players (marked as an example, never in game); two elements never overlap.
• Timer in raids (real raids and the admin test): the same timer as in the levels, counted on the simulation''s steps (the same for the whole group), with the time since the instance began and, under it, the time spent in the zone. It keeps running during a player''s pause (the world never stops); it is an element of the HUD editor''s “Raids” layout (movable, resizable, can be hidden).
• Raid magma: the magma rises are now realistic. The magma rises from the bottom and drains away, drawn over the players and the monsters: nothing shows through it any more, only a glow at its surface above what it hides. Enemies caught in the magma burn like a player would (bosses excepted). New animated lava: a molten body that flows, a dark crust that drifts, bright waves, bubbles that pop, embers, heat, and an alert before each rise (the level it will reach, the ground cracking).
• Right arm: the magma rises more often (every 34 s in the Magma vein, 42 s in the Forge elbow, and now 38 s in the Forearm, with ledges to shelter on), announced 4 s before. Pyroclast''s pits and lava curtains use this new magma too.
• Fix: some symbols were drawn as empty boxes in the raid HUD, the legend of a branch''s map and the titan''s map (ticks, crosses, double arrows, diamonds). They are replaced by signs the game''s fonts have (“OK”, “+”, “◊”, “■”, “◀▶”, “–”); a test now checks that every text of the game, in French and in English, only uses characters its fonts have.' WHERE version = '2.73.2';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.74.1:
• Clan raids: the SHEETS of Asterion and its seven Gigaboss, visible to everyone, even without ever having fought them. They open from CLANS › RAIDS (« Asterion''s sheets »), from the sheet of an event (« Sheets ») and from the lair of each branch map (« … ''s sheet »), even offline.
• Asterion''s sheet: the titan part by part (a part hovered or selected shows its Gigaboss; Enter, A or a click opens its sheet), its story, the raid''s structure (seven branches of eight zones, instances of eight players), what destroying each part takes from it, its cosmic heart — the last fight, once its branches have fallen — and every reward of the raid.
• Each Gigaboss''s sheet: its sprite in each of its three phases, its difficulty from 1 to 10 stars, its phases with their attacks and mechanisms, and each attack or mechanism unfolding with an animated example (its attacks played by the game engine, its mechanisms drawn with the fight''s sprites) and how to avoid it.
• « Mechanisms » tab: what the group must do together (how many players, how long, by the number of players in play), its weak points, its strength by group size and what counts in the contributions. « Place and rewards » tab: its branch, the expedition before its lair, what its fall does to Asterion and its badge.
• Every number of the sheets comes from the rules the fights themselves read: a sheet follows its Gigaboss when its data changes. Boss statistics › Sheet and the raid sheets share the same list of unfolding attacks.

Version 2.74.0:
• Clan raids, phase 6: ASTERION''S HEART, the final fight. Once the seven gigaboss have fallen (validated by the server), the titan''s heart opens on the titan''s map and every group of every clan can fight it at the same time: a long Cosmic aorta for eight (giant ambushes over three floors, locks, a goods lift, checkpoints), then a gigantic arena nine screens wide, its shuttles and ferries turning around a captive star bigger than a screen.
• Its health is shared: each instance plays its own run, but what it tears from the Heart (validated by the consensus of its players) adds up on the server with what every other one took, and each group sees the others'' part taken from it at the same moment on all its screens. It falls for everyone when its shared health is gone: the victory is validated by the server, once, even if two groups strike the last blow together.
• Four phases: “The beating heart”, “The arteries” (hold its four arteries together, two on the floor at the walls and two on high balconies, to bare its three ventricles), “The crown of stars” (a plasma tide burns the floor: stay on the platforms) and a very hard last phase, “Supernova”: at each charge, enough players must hold the anchors at once to contain it, or the whole arena burns.
• Its star lances aim at all eight players at once, its charges cross whole storeys. What the seven branches destroyed really acts on it: the Skull fallen, its lances lose their precision; the Left arm, no more sweeps; the Right arm, no more magma rain; the Torso, no more cage around the heart; the Abdomen, no more spawn; the Left leg, no more gravity traps; the Right leg, its charges slow down. Each relic of the secret zones validated weakens it further. The HUD shows its shared health, its phase, your group''s part and the others'', and a summary of the branches'' effects at the arena''s door.
• Victory: the film “The fall of Asterion” (the titan collapses, its heart becomes a supernova, the clans'' banners rise) starts for the whole group as soon as the server validates the fall, then can be watched again from the event''s sheet (“Watch the victory again”).
• Rewards, each granted once by the server: the “Asterion''s Heart” badge (present at its fall), the “Asterion''s Supernova” victory effect (one minute of validated fight in its arena), the “Asterion''s Heart” profile frame for the 10 best contribution scores of the event (the mixed score, never the damage alone) and the collective clan title “Star Breakers” for each clan present at the fall. The world event only announces “Asterion has fallen” with the seven gigaboss AND the heart; registered players are told when the heart opens and when it falls.
• ADMINISTRATION › Raids › “Test Asterion”: Asterion''s Heart can be tested, with its starting phase (1 to 4), the parts of the titan to simulate as fallen (to see their effects) and the relics; a test never reports anything. It plays like a real instance, with the simulated players.
• HUD editor › “Raids”: two new elements, “Heart''s shared health” (what is left for every group, your part, the others'' part, its phase) and “Effects of the branches on the Heart” (shown at its arena''s door), placed, resized or hidden like the others. The list of elements switches to two columns when one does not fit on the screen.' WHERE version = '2.74.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.74.2:
• Fix: Asterion''s sheet counted the Heart as an eighth branch (8 branches, 57 zones); it shows the seven branches, their 56 zones and 7 lairs again, the Heart being presented on its own.' WHERE version = '2.74.2';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.75.0:
• Clan raids: new “What is left to do” panel (raid HUD, movable and resizable in Settings › HUD › “Raids”): every condition to finish the zone (“1 generator of 2”, “Open the way in: …”, “Ambush 2 of 4”, the plates to hold together), ticked as soon as the server validated it (“waiting for the server''s validation” while only your group did it), then what is missing in every other zone of the branch.
• Large map (M): each zone shows its state (finished, to finish, locked, zone to take back) and, until it is finished, what it misses.
• Zone finished: at the same moment, every player of the instance sees the “ZONE FINISHED” card with a sound, whether their group or another one finished it; the branch''s other zones finished elsewhere are announced in the alerts, and the titan''s alerts (titan map) write it once per zone.
• Contributions table of each zone: at the end of a zone, each player''s share of the damage dealt to the zone''s boss and mini-bosses (guardians, enemies whose fall is an objective, Gigaboss), their damage, support, mechanisms and objectives, counted by the simulation (the same numbers on every game of the group); sent to the server and validated by the group''s majority, it stays in “Raid results” (“Zone tables”) and can be seen again from the pause.
• Gigaboss sheets: new “Where to hit” diagram in the “Mechanisms” tab: the Gigaboss''s real sprite for the chosen phase and state (fight, armoured, bare), with its areas read from the fight''s own rules: to hit (green), armoured (grey), what hurts on contact or attacks (red), the collective mechanism''s plates in the arena (gold), a measured legend and “Hit here when…”.
• Administration: for moderation, administrators see the real presence and hidden profiles (marked “hidden”) in ADMINISTRATION › Players, clan members and raid registrants; the server sends this to signed-in administrators only, never to other players. No precise location is ever collected and the country stays hidden unless the player shows it. Online settings: the explanation of “hide” says so.
• ADMINISTRATION › Players: each row unfolds (“+”: click, Enter or A) and shows the player''s latest levels played, newest first: the level, the date, their best time (crystals, under verification) or their play time, their attempts and “Watch” when a verified replay exists; pages of ten. The data is the server''s, given to administrators only and written to the Log.
• An administrator can watch a verified replay despite a hidden profile or an inactive account (checked by the server from the session''s role): “Viewed as admin (hidden profile)” stays shown during playback and the Log notes it; an incomplete replay or one of another version of the level is still refused with its reason, and other players keep exactly their locks.' WHERE version = '2.75.0';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.75.1:
• Raids: a downed player comes back as many times as a teammate revives them (2 s near their soul). If the WHOLE group falls, it is out of the zone for good: no restart nor checkpoint, the zone is not validated and its players become spectators (« GROUP WIPED OUT — spectator mode »: free camera, the branch''s next / previous player). Coming back from the menu never gives a seat again, only the spectator''s view.
• Raids: a zone where a group was wiped out is « to take back » on the branch''s map; a group that finished its own zone takes it back (« Take this zone back ») in a fresh instance of that zone, the branch''s validated state kept, and only that group validates it.
• Raids: each branch starts with an armory where everyone takes the powers they want for the raid (one tablet per power, four at most: the choice window asks which one to leave), then the whole group on the « Ready » plate opens the route.
• Raids and co-op: players pass through each other (no more solid players nor standing on an ally) and the other players, real or simulated, are drawn semi-transparent with an outline of their colour; only your character stays opaque.
• Raids and co-op: when a player falls, nobody else moves nor reappears at the last checkpoint; they come back only once revived, near their soul. In co-op, revivals stay limited to 2 per attempt. Earlier Duo/Trio attempts replay identically and their records are kept; the server refuses attempts played with older rules.
• Raids: the magma and the other rising liquids fill their whole basin (at least the screen''s width, from one rock rim to the other), always in front of the players and the enemies.
• Fix (« Test Asterion »): a simulated player''s fall sent the administrator back to the start; only the administrator is invincible, the simulated players fall, revive each other and can be wiped out like a real group.
• « Test Asterion »: « Simulated players: 0 (just you) … 7 », the administrator not counted (before, choosing 2 gave a single simulated player).' WHERE version = '2.75.1';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.75.3:
• Moderation: an administrator sees all of a player''s profile, even hidden or of an inactive account: statistics, time played, achievements, outfit, badges and title, private followers and follows, drafts and levels hidden by reports, best progressions. The server decides from the role of their session, never from a parameter; other players keep exactly their locks.
• Profile seen by an administrator: a discreet “Viewed as admin” mark on everything that would be hidden from others (header, tabs, unpublished levels), and a new “Admin” tab: privacy settings, real presence and last activity, friends (their profile opens from there) and friend requests, pending clan requests (without their message), and every record sent with its status and “Watch”.
• Unverified records, attempts and replays (pending, rejected): visible to administrators for moderation, always marked (“Viewed as admin (awaiting verification)” during playback) and never counted as verified records. A replay never sent or incomplete, or of another version of the level, stays unavailable with its reason.
• What stays hidden, even from an administrator: a country or region the player hides (only the setting is told), any precise position, passwords and other secrets, and private messages between players.
• Administration log: each view of a normally hidden profile or replay is written there, grouped into one entry per player while they follow each other within an hour (“3 views, the last one on …”, with the locks lifted and the levels seen). Online settings: the privacy explanation says what administrators see.

Version 2.75.2:
• Asterion''s sheets: the « Where to hit » diagram now shows each attack on its real animation. Under the phases and states, pick a pose (« At rest » or an attack of the phase): the Gigaboss plays its wind-up then its blow, and the diagram shows what comes out of it (red: what hurts, such as the rush, the impact and its shockwaves, the crown of flames; pink: where its shots and beams come from).
• Asterion''s sheets: the weak points and targets are drawn with their own sprite, where the fight sticks them (Skullmaw''s eyes and crystal, Pyroclast''s knuckles, Titanus''s knee and restraints…); a cross marks the Gigaboss''s feet, where everything is measured from. Fix: Heartbreaker''s four plates are the armour of its first phase (the diagram showed them in phase 2).
• Raids: the Gigaboss''s shots and beams finally leave their drawing, no longer 80 to 300 px above them: Skullmaw''s gaze, Pyroclast''s bombs, Heartbreaker''s clots, the Voidworm''s spit, the beam of Asterion''s Heart. The crown of flames of Heartbreaker, Graviton and the Heart keeps its radius (it circled much further out). Other enemies do not change and no record is erased.
• Raids: the Gigaboss rules change (shots and crown), so a raid instance only brings together players on 2.75.2 or later: update the game to join your group.' WHERE version = '2.75.3';
UPDATE client_releases SET notes_en = 'Version 2.76.0:
• Bosses: each boss is cut into parts that follow its drawing frame by frame (head, neck, body, wings, tail, legs, claws, breath for Pyrrhax; the body for the others), instead of a single box. The shapes are drawn from the sprites of its 94 sheets by a tool, to the pixel.
• Pyrrhax fights by parts: its head is a weak point (× 2), its tail is armoured (× 0.5), its neck, body, wings and legs take the hits normally. You can hit it at the tip of a wing, far beyond its old box. Only its claws, its breath and its head while biting hurt on contact. Earlier replays play again exactly and no record is erased.
• Boss sheets: new « Where to hit » tab (STATISTICS › a boss). It shows the real sprite with a chip per phase and a chip per pose (rest, wind-up, attack…), its parts on the current frame, and a legend with the role and damage of each part. The sheets of Asterion''s Gigaboss show their parts too.
• Fleeing enemies: a weakened enemy no longer goes further than 5.5 tiles from where it started fleeing, and a flying enemy no longer rises more than 2 tiles above it. At that limit it is cornered: it faces you, attacks or guards if it can, and can be hit. Ghosts no longer end up on the ceiling or off screen. Enemy editor: « Max flee distance ».' WHERE version = '2.76.0';
